>  I'll say to myself: ".i mi mi tavla dei (I love
> using "dei") .i mi ri tavla .i mi ri fa mi ri fa mi ri fa mi ri tavla
> dei"  (I'm to me I'm to me I'm to me I'm to me talking about this
> sentence!  But the Lojban is grammatical! [.uisai] Wee!)

I think what you're actually saying is that you're talking to the first
sentence, because {ri} skips {mi} and ends up pointing to the
first {dei}. Or perhaps you are talking to the word "dei", if the inserted
sentence in English also counts. I never remember exactly which
sumti {ri} ignores,but I think {mi} is one of them.

mu'o mi'e xorxes


